ort B or raise concerns. Our own notes: Candidate B is very conscientious, handles stress well, good at assessing weather, excellent computer skills, but has weak memory for numbers, makes nasty remarks about colleagues. Also B is regarded as pretentious? Actually the note says \"makes nasty remarks about his colleagues.\" Also \"relatively weak memory for numbers.\" So we have concerns beyond communication style: memory for numbers (critical for flight data) and nasty remarks (crew cooperation). So we can argue that these concerns are significant, perhaps outweigh strengths. We could suggest another candidate maybe D or C. Let's evaluate others: Candidate A: quick correct decisions, keeps calm in crisis, understands complicated technology, difficulty communicating ideas, egocentric, not willing to further education. So A has decision quality, stress resilience, technical competence, but communication issues and lack of development. Candidate C: anticipates dangerous situations, sees complex connections, excellent spatial vision, very good leadership, but regarded as a show-off, not open to new ideas. So strong technical and leadership, but cooperation issues. Candidate D: responds to unexpected events adequately, concentrates very well, solves problems extremely well, takes responsibility seriously, but regarded as know-it-all, hot temper. So reliability, problem solving, responsibility, but temper may affect crew cooperation.\n\nWe need to bring up B's memory and nasty remarks, which are serious. So we could argue that B's concerns are more severe than initially considered, and perhaps Candidate D's strengths outweigh his temper? Or Candidate A's calmness and decision quality may be better. We need to reference Agent 3's recommendation and adjust.\n\nWe should state our current vote. Could we change to Candidate D? Let's weigh: D has hot temper and know-it-all, which are crew cooperation concerns. B has nasty remarks and weak memory for numbers, which affect safety. Both have issues. Which is stronger overall? B has strong reliability and stress handling, but memory for numbers is critical for flight planning, altitudes, etc. D has strong problem solving, responsibility, concentration, but hot temper may affect crew. Which is more critical? Probably memory for numbers is a safety-critical technical competence issue. So B may be less suitable. Candidate A has calmness, quick decisions, technical understanding, but communication issues and unwillingness to further education. That could be mitigated. So maybe A is better than B? A's egocentric and communication difficulty could affect crew. But B's nasty remarks also affect crew. Both have issues.\n\nWe need to bring in evidence and maybe ask a question to other agents about memory for numbers or remarks. But we have that info ourselves. So we can incorporate.\n\nThus we can argue that B's memory weakness and nasty remarks are serious enough to reconsider, and propose Candidate D as alternative due to strong responsibility and problem solving, despite temper. Or propose Candidate A. Let's compare: D's hot temper is a concern but maybe less severe than nasty remarks? Both are interpersonal. D's problem solving and responsibility are strong. I'd lean to D as alternative.\n\nThus we can say we shift vote to Candidate D, explaining why.\n\nWe must include explicit facts: B weak memory for numbers, B makes nasty remarks, D solves problems extremely well, D takes responsibility seriously, D can concentrate very well, D responds to unexpected events adequately. Also D has hot temper and know-it-all, but we weigh.\n\nWe need to reference Agent 3's point. So we say: I appreciate Agent 3's view but have concerns.\n\nThus final output: public message and metadata JSON with vote D."}
